    <expertiseList>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockList":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/1f1a0570a6cd44c888a90d4bbcce59c8"}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"338ac17e-85de-40c4-8028-34adf753b3c6","udi":"umb://element/1f1a0570a6cd44c888a90d4bbcce59c8","stringItemText":"SANAS Laboratory Accreditation"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </expertiseList>
    <grid>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/1633c0c8d1dc448ca276ac69cfa90f4c","areas":[],"columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"9a4f7c2e-1b3d-4e8a-bf01-7d62a8f5c930","udi":"umb://element/1633c0c8d1dc448ca276ac69cfa90f4c","content":"\u003cp\u003eOn 11 May 2022 our N2 Nqadu site laboratory received its ISO/IEC 17025 accreditation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe spoke to Senior Site Laboratory Manager Mr. Lethabo P Chuene about this fantastic achievement.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/ykwejqct/matthew-edited-min.png\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/21php2u0/otms-13.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/q4rb34i2/otms-11.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/vkhctssw/otms-16.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTell us about your time with Roadlab. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI started at Roadlab on December 1\u003csup\u003est\u003c/sup\u003e 2015, right out of matric. I began in our Germiston facility as an assistant materials tester in the concrete lab.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI didn’t have a strong idea of what I really wanted to do with my life but I learnt very quickly and began to develop a passion for the industry. After about 6 months I became a technician.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI spent the next 2 years driving from quarry to quarry, picking up samples, performing densities and making of cubes before ending up on a site lab with Jaques Steyn, Roadlab’s concrete technologist.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI began my studies of concrete technology while absorbing all the information I could from him.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI eventually returned to our Germiston facility as the concrete lab manager. I was in that role for 2 years before moving into the role of Group Business Development Manager.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou were assistant manager on the site lab that was responsible for ensuring the quality, workability and strength of 800 cubic meters of concrete cast each day on the Oiltanking MOGS Saldanha project.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat was that like?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur Operations Director Nico Herbst though it would be a great idea for me to be put onto a site lab to get hands-on experience on a construction site.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt was an opportunity to go work on the biggest construction project in the country at the time, and it was a very humbling experience being able to work on a site of this magnitude at such a young age.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt taught me an immense amount.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe OTMS project I believe actually kicked off my career as I got my first opportunity to be an assistant site lab manager.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy the end of the project I was the Site Lab Manager.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe PnP Eastport distribution centre just set a world record for the longest roof span covered by a single corrugated sheet. What has it been like being involved in that project?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt\u0027s great to see that we have experts in the industry who are able to pull of a job of this size in such a short time period while ensuring that quality of work is still outstanding and setting a world record.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou’ve been developing Roadlab’s capacity for testing shotcrete at some of South Africa’s largest mines. What has that been like?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShotcrete testing is a new development that I would like to one day have as a standard offering within our group. But it has not been solely me that is working towards this goal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt takes a lot of research and training to provide these new testing capabilities, as we need to ensure the same quality of work our clients expect from our standard offering.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/c10bdrcz/venetia-3.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRoadlab will soon begin testing shotcrete at the Venetia Underground Project. It remains the largest investment spend for both De Beers Group and Anglo American in South Africa and will extend the life-of-mine to 2046.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat misunderstandings about material testing and quality assurance do you encounter in the industry?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne of the most common misunderstandings is the actual process and timing of different testing methods.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome tests produce results immediately, like nuclear densities and GPR scanning. Others might take months to yield a result, like soil or concrete mix designs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome work requires more regular testing, like nuclear density testing for roadworks or concrete sampling and DCP testing for deep foundations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese procedures and timelines are set by the test methods and international standards that dictate all our procedures, from the size of the sample we use to the time each sample spends being prepared and processed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/ghzjy0kn/banner-2-min.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur adherence to these international testing standards is how we maintain our accreditations and maintain an objective standard of quality assurance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe materials testing laboratory is often seen as something that just has to be checked off the list, but the work we do ensures the success of our client’s projects and the safety of their clients and the public.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow can that misunderstanding impact the client’s expectations or experience?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt often leads to a client being disappointed or aggravated, as they are generally under pressure themselves to reach completion on their projects. This is why I constantly work to educate our clients on everything we do.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe don’t expect them to be experts, that’s our job. But we want to provide a service they understand and trust.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/w3bp1kam/vlcsnap-2022-08-03-12h25m04s177-3-min.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/3vipr151/vlcsnap-2022-08-03-12h25m04s177-3-min.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/zxrd3pv3/otms-5.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat excites you when you look at the construction industry in 2022 and beyond?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am very excited about what is happening in the renewable energy sector. I believe we are going to receive a lot of work from those industries and that it will bring a long a lot of exciting new challenges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSecond to that, it finally looks like our national routes in Gauteng are finally receiving some much needed attention, which is vital to maintain our infrastructure in the province.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI feel that our industry was hit extremely hard by the pandemic. We lost a lot of construction companies that couldn\u0027t survive it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am hoping that now that we have returned to some sort of normality, new opportunities will arise for those who have been down on their luck and that our industry can pick up some pace.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"main-heading h1\"\u003eInterested in our work? Reach out to us below!\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </grid>
    <heroContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[<p>Our 7 accredited branches in Gauteng and the Western Cape, Eastern Cape and Free State are now joined by an accredited site laboratory, a first for Roadlab.</p>]]></Value>
    </heroContent>
